ein in the axonal transport of microtubules and neurofilaments. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>168</volume>:<fpage>697</fpage>&#x02013;703.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15728192</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Kapitein, L.C., E.J. Peterman, B.H. Kwok, J.H. Kim, T.M. Kapoor, and C.F. Schmidt. <year>2005</year>. The bipolar mitotic kinesin Eg5 moves on both microtubules that it crosslinks. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>435</volume>:<fpage>114</fpage>&#x02013;118.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15875026</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Kapoor, T.M., T.U. Mayer, M.L. Coughlin, and T.J. Mitchison. <year>2000</year>. Probing spindle assembly mechanisms with monastrol, a small molecule inhibitor of the mitotic kinesin, Eg5. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>150</volume>:<fpage>975</fpage>&#x02013;988.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10973989</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Kashina, A.S., R.J. Baskin, D.G. Cole, K.P. Wedaman, W.M. Saxton, and J.M. Scholey. <year>1996</year>. A bipolar kinesin. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>379</volume>:<fpage>270</fpage>&#x02013;272.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8538794</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Kwok, B.H., L.C. Kapitein, J.H. Kim, E.J. Peterman, C.F. Schmidt, and T.M. Kapoor. <year>2006</year>. Allosteric inhibition of kinesin-5 modulates its processive directional motility. <source>Nat Chem Biol.</source> <volume>2</volume>:<fpage>480</fpage>&#x02013;485.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16892050</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Lockhart, A., and R.A. Cross. <year>1996</year>. Kinetics and motility of the Eg5 microtubule motor. <source>Biochemistry.</source> <volume>35</volume>:<fpage>2365</fpage>&#x02013;2373.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8652578</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Ma, Y., D. Shakiryanova, I. Vardya, and S.V. Popov. <year>2004</year>. Quantitative analysis of microtubule transport in growing nerve processes. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>14</volume>:<fpage>725</fpage>&#x02013;730.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15084289</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Maliga, Z., and T.J. Mitchison. <year>2006</year>. Small-molecule and mutational analysis of allosteric Eg5 inhibition by monastrol. <source>BMC Chem. Biol.</source> <volume>6</volume>:<fpage>2</fpage>.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16504166</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Maliga, Z., T.M. Kapoor, and T.J. Mitchison. <year>2002</year>. Evidence that monastrol is an allosteric inhibitor of the mitotic kinesin Eg5. <source>Chem. Biol.</source> <volume>9</volume>:<fpage>989</fpage>&#x02013;996.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12323373</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><citation citation-type="journal">Mountain, V., C. Simerly, L. Howard, A. Ando, G. Schatten, and D.A. Compton. <year>1999</year>. The kinesin-related protein, HSET, opposes the activity of Eg5 and cross-links microtubules in the mammalian mitotic spindle. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>147</volume>:<fpage>351</fpage>&#x02013;366.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10525540</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><citation citation-type="journal">Myers, K.A., Y. He, T.P. Hasaka, and P.W. Baas. <year>2006</year>a. Microtubule transport in the axon: re-thinking a potential role for the actin cytoskeleton. <source>Neuroscientist.</source> <volume>12</volume>:<fpage>107</fpage>&#x02013;118.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16514008</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib29"><citation citation-type="journal">Myers, K.A., I. Tint, C.V. Nadar, Y. He, M.M. Black, and P.W. Baas. <year>2006</year>b. Antagonistic forces generated by cytoplasmic dynein and myosin-II during growth cone turning and axonal retraction. <source>Traffic.</source> <volume>7</volume>:<fpage>1333</fpage>&#x02013;1351.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16911591</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib30"><citation citation-type="journal">Pfister, K.K. <year>1999</year>. Cytoplasmic dynein and microtubule transport in the axon: the action connection. <source>Mol. Neurobiol.</source> <volume>20</volume>:<fpage>81</fpage>&#x02013;91.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10966115</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib31"><citation citation-type="journal">Saunders, A.M., J. Powers, S. Strome, and W.M. Saxton. <year>2007</year>. Kinesin-5 acts as a brake in anaphase spindle elongation. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>17</volume>:<fpage>R453</fpage>&#x02013;R454.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17580072</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib32"><citation citation-type="journal">Sawin, K.E., and T.J. Mitchison. <year>1995</year>. Mutations in the kinesin-like protein Eg5 disrupting localization to the mitotic spindle. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>92</volume>:<fpage>4289</fpage>&#x02013;4293.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7753799</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib33"><citation citation-type="journal">Sharp, D.J., R. Kuriyama, R. Essner, and P.W. Baas. <year>1997</year>. Expression of a minus-end-directed motor protein induces Sf9 cells to form axon-like processes with uniform microtubule polarity orientation. <source>J. Cell Sci.</source> <volume>110</volume>:<fpage>2373</fpage>&#x02013;2380.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9410876</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib34"><citation citation-type="journal">Sharp, D.J., K.L. McDonald, H.M. Brown, H.J. Matthies, C. Walczak, R.D. Vale, T.J. Mitchison, and J.M. Scholey. <year>1999</year>a. The bipolar kinesin, KLP61F, cross-links microtubules within interpolar microtubule bundles of <italic>Drosophila</italic> embryonic mitotic spindles. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>144</volume>:<fpage>125</fpage>&#x02013;138.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9885249</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib35"><citation citation-type="journal">Sharp, D.J., K.R. Yu, J.C. Sisson, W. Sullivan, and J.M. Scholey. <year>1999</year>b. Antagonistic microtubule-sliding motors position mitotic centrosomes in <italic>Drosophila</italic> early embryos. <source>Nat. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>1</volume>:<fpage>51</fpage>&#x02013;54.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10559864</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib36"><citation citation-type="journal">Tao, L., A. Mogilner, G. Civelekoglu-Scholey, R. Wollman, J. Evans, H. Stahlberg, and J.M. Scholey. <year>2006</year>. A homotetrameric kinesin-5, KLP61F, bundles microtubules and antagonizes Ncd in motility assays. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>16</volume>:<fpage>2293</fpage>&#x02013;2302.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17141610</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib37"><citation citation-type="journal">Walczak, C.E., I. Vernos, T.J. Mitchison, E. Karsenti, and R. Heald. <year>1998</year>. A model for the proposed roles of different microtubule-based motor proteins in establishing spindle bipolarity. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>8</volume>:<fpage>903</fpage>&#x02013;913.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9707401</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib38"><citation citation-type="journal">Wang, L., and A. Brown. <year>2002</year>. Rapid movement of microtubules in axons. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>12</volume>:<fpage>1496</fpage>&#x02013;1501.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12225664</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib39"><citation citation-type="journal">Weil, D., L. Garcon, M. Harper, D. Dumenil, F. Dautry, and M. Kress. <year>2002</year>. Targeting the kinesin Eg5 to monitor siRNA transfection in mammalian cells. <source>Biotechniques.</source> <volume>33</volume>:<fpage>1244</fpage>&#x02013;1248.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12503308</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib40"><citation citation-type="journal">Yoon, S.Y., J.E. Choi, J.W. Huh, O. Hwang, H.S. Lee, H.N. Hong, and D. Kim. <year>2005</year>. Monastrol, a selective inhibitor of the mitotic kinesin Eg5, induces a distinctive growth profile of dendrites and axons in primary cortical neuron cultures. <source>Cell Motil. Cytoskeleton.</source> <volume>60</volume>:<fpage>181</fpage>&#x02013;190.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15751098</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib41"><citation citation-type="journal">Yu, W., and P.W. Baas. <year>1994</year>. Changes in microtubule number and length during axon differentiation. <source>J. Neurosci.</source> <volume>14</volume>:<fpage>2818</fpage>&#x02013;2829.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8182441</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib42"><citation citation-type="journal">Yu, W., J.M. Solowska, L. Qiang, A. Karabay, D. Baird, and P.W. Baas. <year>2005</year>. Regulation of microtubule severing by katanin subunits during neuronal development. <source>J. Neurosci.</source> <volume>25</volume>:<fpage>5573</fpage>&#x02013;5583.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15944385</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>